The Django application in appointments-app/ was provided by the Amazon Cloud
Institute (ACI) as starter code for Capstone 2. All source in that directory
is the work of ACI, not of this repository's author.

This remains true of the Lab 3 changes inside appointments-app/ — the DynamoDB
announcements read in appointments/views.py, the announcements block in
appointments/templates/appointments/index.html, and the mock_scan and
test_announcements additions in appointments/tests.py. Those follow ACI lab
instructions and are ACI's content. The author's own edits in that directory are
incidental adaptations for local tooling and CI: reading the table name from the
ANNOUNCEMENTS_TABLE environment variable, the PYTHONPATH prefix in
local_build.sh, and the corresponding fixes in buildspec_unittest.yml (the
PYTHONPATH prefix, the $CODEBUILD_SRC_DIR phase paths, the report
base-directory entries, and the Python 3.12 runtime).

Everything in infrastructure/ is the original work of this repository's author:
the Terraform module and environment layout, the DynamoDB table configuration,
the CodeBuild project module and its GitHub source wiring, and the S3 remote
state backend.

Any further files added by the repository author will be noted here as they are
introduced.
